'''''Echium creticum''''', the '''Cretan viper's bugloss''', ([[synonym (taxonomy)|syn.]] ''Echium calycinum'' [[Viv.]], ''Echium rubrum'' [[Conrad Moench|Moench]], ''Echium sericeum'' [[Martin Vahl|Vahl]], ''Echium violaceum'' [[Carl Linnaeus|L.]]) is a species of [[flowering plant]] in the family [[Boraginaceae]]. It is native to the western [[Mediterranean Basin]].<ref>{{cite web |title=Echium creticum |url=http://www.floraiberica.es/floraiberica/texto/pdfs/11_138_16_Echium.pdf |publisher=[[Flora Iberica]] |access-date=23 July 2022}}</ref> It is also used as an [[ornamental plant]].

